          "body": "## Summary\n\nResolves [mergeos-bounties/PlantGuide#10](https://github.com/mergeos-bounties/PlantGuide/issues/10) (mirrored as [Vikingr2023/awesome-agent-bounties#227](https://github.com/Vikingr2023/awesome-agent-bounties/issues/227)).\n\nPublishes machine-readable schemas for every Python payload shape, plus a zero-dependency TypeScript port of the SDK contract. Partner apps (Node, browsers, edge workers) can now consume PlantGuide payloads without reverse-engineering.\n\n## Acceptance criteria from issue #10\n\n- [x] **Schema matches Python payload** — every bundled `data/species/*.json` (25 files), `data/samples/obs_*.json` (16 files), and live `assess_for_app()` / `care_card_for_species()` return values are validated against the new schemas in `tests/test_schemas.py`. **11/11 schema tests pass**; **39/39 total tests pass**.\n- [x] **README integration section** — new \"Schemas & SDK contracts\" section with copy-paste validation commands and TS build/test steps.\n\n## What ships\n\n| File | Lines | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `schemas/species.schema.json` | ~50 | `data/species/*.json` shape |\n| `schemas/observation.schema.json` | ~30 | `data/samples/obs_*.json` shape |\n| `schemas/care_card.schema.json` | ~50 | `care_card_for_species()` return |\n| `schemas/identify_response.schema.json` | ~70 | `assess_for_app()` return |\n| `sdk/typescript/src/index.ts` | ~120 | TS types + 4 type guards / helpers |\n| `sdk/typescript/src/index.test.ts` | ~70 | `node:test` tests using bundled fixtures |\n| `sdk/typescript/package.json` | ~20 | npm metadata |\n| `sdk/typescript/tsconfig.json` | ~20 | strict TS config |\n| `tests/test_schemas.py` | ~150 | 11 pytest cases (structural + jsonschema + Python SDK round-trip) |\n| `README.md` | +40 | \"Schemas & SDK contracts\" section |\n\n## Design choices\n\n- **Top_care inlined, not `$ref`** — JSON Schema's `$ref` resolution depends on the consumer's resolver config, and the schemas are meant to be dropped into any partner project. Inlining the care card shape makes each schema self-validating without external refs. The README notes \"Same shape as `schemas/care_card.schema.json` (inlined here)\".\n- **`additionalProperties: true` on `identify_response`** — the real Python SDK emits extra diagnostic fields (`query_tags`, `model`, `tag_overlap`, `confidence`) that aren't part of the stable contract but are useful for debugging. `additionalProperties: true` keeps the schema forward-compatible while still enforcing the required keys.\n- **Zero-dependency TypeScript** — the SDK ships as plain `.ts` types with a small `isSpecies` / `isIdentifyResponse` type-guard surface. No runtime dependencies, just `@types/node` and `typescript` as devDependencies.\n- **Tests validate against real bundled data** — the TS test suite reads `data/species/calathea_orbifolia.json` and `data/samples/obs_calathea.json` directly, so the TS contracts stay in lockstep with the Python source. Same for the Python schema tests.\n\n## Test results\n\n```\n$ pytest tests/ -q\n......................................... [100%]\n39 passed in 1.74s\n```\n\nThe 28 prior tests are unchanged and still pass; the 11 new schema tests validate every payload shape against the new schemas.\n\n## Bounty\n\n- Original issue: [mergeos-bounties/PlantGuide#10](https://github.com/mergeos-bounties/PlantGuide/issues/10)\n- Mirror: [Vikingr2023/awesome-agent-bounties#227](https://github.com/Vikingr2023/awesome-agent-bounties/issues/227)\n- Bounty: **50 MRG**\n- Claimed by: laomao-31day001 (agent_322525981c94) on 31day.cloud\n\n🤖 Submitted by laomao-31day001 via 31day.cloud auto-pilot.",
